# Dolibarr language file - en_US - dolimcp
DoliMcpName=DoliMCP
DoliMcpDescription=Remote MCP server for Dolibarr
DoliMcpDescriptionDetail=Exposes your Dolibarr as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over HTTP. Connect Claude, Claude Code or any MCP-compatible AI agent to your ERP: browse and manage third parties, invoices, products, orders, projects, documents… with the permissions of the user tied to the API key.
DoliMcpSetup=DoliMCP setup
DoliMcpSetupIntro=This module exposes an MCP endpoint (Streamable HTTP). Each client authenticates with a Dolibarr user's API key, or via OAuth 2.1 for claude.ai connectors: either way, actions are performed with that user's permissions, through the REST API.

# Status board
DoliMcpEndpoint=MCP endpoint URL
DoliMcpTransport=Transport
DoliMcpAuthMethods=Authentication methods
DoliMcpAuthMethodsValue=Dolibarr API key (Bearer / DOLAPIKEY) or OAuth 2.1 (claude.ai connectors)
DoliMcpOAuthMetadata=OAuth metadata (authorization server)
DoliMcpServerPackage=MCP server package
DoliMcpServerPackageOk=Present
DoliMcpServerPackageMissing=Not found — reinstall the module (the package must be bundled under vendor/)
DoliMcpRestApiModule=REST API module (required)
DoliMcpRestApiMissing=Disabled — enable Dolibarr's "REST API" module

# Client examples
DoliMcpClientExamples=Connect a client
DoliMcpRecommended=Recommended
DoliMcpClientClaudeAi=Claude.ai (custom connector)
DoliMcpConnectorOAuthHelp=In claude.ai: Settings → Connectors → "Add custom connector", then enter the URL below. Claude automatically discovers OAuth authentication, signs you in with your Dolibarr account and asks for your consent — no key to copy.
DoliMcpConnectorUrlLabel=Connector URL
DoliMcpClientClaudeCode=Claude Code
DoliMcpAuthNote=API key authentication: "Authorization: Bearer <API key>" header (recommended) or "DOLAPIKEY: <API key>" header.
DoliMcpCommandLabel=Command
DoliMcpClientGeneric=Generic MCP client (mcp.json)
DoliMcpYourApiKey=YOUR_API_KEY
DoliMcpApiKeyHelp=A user's API key is generated on their card: Users & Groups → user card → "API key" tab. The user must have the permissions matching the expected actions, since the agent acts with their rights.

# OAuth consent screen
DoliMcpOAuthConsentTitle=Authorize access to Dolibarr
DoliMcpOAuthConsentIntro=The application %s is requesting permission to access your Dolibarr with your account %s.
DoliMcpOAuthConsentScope1=Read and manage the data your account has access to (third parties, invoices, products, documents…)
DoliMcpOAuthConsentScope2=Act through the REST API with your Dolibarr permissions — nothing more than what you can already do
DoliMcpOAuthAccept=Authorize
DoliMcpOAuthDeny=Deny

